  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Living the call of Pope Francis Laudato Si&#x2019; Encyclical in the AMECEA Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is as a result of the 20th Association of Member Episcopal Conferences in Eastern Africa (AMECEA) Plenary Assembly held in Tanzania from 9th to 18th July 2022, that focused on the central message of Pope Francis&#x2019; landmark encyclical, Laudato Si&#x2019; on care for our common home. During the AMECEA 20th Plenary assembly closing mass one of the documents launched was the AMECEA region Laudato Si&#x2019; implementations guidelines based on Laudato Si&#x2019; action platform seven goals. The AMECEA Laudato Si&#x2019; guidelines were development after a series of assessments, research and review of best practices with support of CAFOD funding in the year 2019/2020 and 2021/2022. Through the process of developing the guidelines major challenges and gaps were identified in implementing Pope Francis Laudato Si&#x2019; in the AMECEA region, hence the need to develop the guidelines that will help the implementation at all levels of the Catholic Church from the national conferences, dioceses up to the Small Christian Communities.</narrative>
  </description>
